<section id="method">
  <div class="eyebrow">How this was built</div>
  <h2>Method and caveats</h2>
  <div class="notes">
    <p><strong>Hard data first.</strong> Where a number exists, it drives the score: 2025 KNRUHS closing ranks, NMC seat matrices, college-disclosed bed and OPD counts, university pass rates, and the NMC stipend list. Softer parameters (faculty quality, PG-prep culture, abroad pathway) are judgement calls based on student reviews and NMC remarks, so treat them as ±1.</p>
    <p><strong>Forums.</strong> See the "What forums say" section. Review sites skew positive and have small samples, so the NMC and KNRUHS records get more weight than any single review.</p>
    <p><strong>No college runs a formal USMLE programme.</strong> That score is a proxy: hospital brand recognition, international-patient exposure and research output.</p>
    <p><strong>Fees.</strong> Telangana kept the 2023–26 tuition for the 2026–29 block (G.O.Ms.No.98, 07.08.2026): Apollo and Kamineni ₹13 L/yr, SVS ₹12.5 L, both Mamatas ₹12 L. Hostel, mess and the KNRUHS university fee are extra. Confirm with the college before paying.</p>
    <p><strong>Discontinuation.</strong> Leaving after the cut-off date triggers the ₹20 lakh bond and a 3-year debarment from Telangana MBBS admission, so settle your choice now, not after joining.</p>
    <p><strong>Not advice.</strong> This is a structured comparison to support your decision, not a guarantee of allotment or outcomes. Always check the live KNRUHS notification.</p>
